idation that the query_id belongs to the requesting user. Unprotected real-time agent communication channel.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-863: Incorrect Authorization\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Require authentication before accepting WebSocket connections. Validate query ownership per connection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api/websocket.py\",\n      \"line\": 98,\n      \"description\": \"WebSocket receives JSON without schema validation before processing. Malformed or malicious input could cause crashes or unexpected behavior.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-1025: Comparison Using Wrong Factors\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Use Pydantic models to validate incoming WebSocket messages: `msg = WSQuery.model_validate(data)`\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"file\": \"src/main.py\",\n      \"line\": \"18-20\",\n      \"description\": \"No HTTPS/TLS enforcement. Server runs on plain HTTP (0.0.0.0:8000). All HR policy data and user queries transmitted unencrypted over the network.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Deploy behind HTTPS reverse proxy (nginx/Caddy). Use ASGI server with SSL: uvicorn --ssl-keyfile --ssl-certfile\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api/routes.py\",\n      \"line\": \"130, 160, 173, 186\",\n      \"description\": \"Error messages leak internal information. HTTPException returns full error strings (str(e)) which could expose system paths, database details, or LLM configuration to attackers.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-209: Information Exposure Through an Error Message\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Return generic error messages to clients. Log full errors server-side only. Use custom exception handlers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/llm/client.py\",\n      \"line\": 63,\n      \"description\": \"Debug logging of raw LLM responses (logger.debug('Raw response: %s', raw)). This could log sensitive HR policy information or user queries to log files accessible to attackers.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-532: Insertion of Sensitive Information into Log File\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Never log raw user input or LLM responses. Log only sanitized summaries and error codes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/fetch/engine.py\",\n      \"line\": 72-75,\n      \"description\": \"URL normalization with regex (re.search) modifies URLs without validating results. Could be exploited to bypass URL restrictions or cause unexpected fetches.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-95: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Use urllib.parse for URL parsing. Maintain an explicit allowlist of governement policy domains.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/data/db.py\",\n      \"line\": \"19\",\n      \"description\": \"Hardcoded relative database path. Running the app from different directories could create multiple database instances or cause permission issues. Could be exploited for path traversal.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-426: Untrusted Search Path\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Use absolute paths or environment variables: db_path = Path(os.environ.get('DATA_DIR', './data')) / 'hr_policy_agent.db'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/main.py\",\n      \"line\": \"42-51\",\n      \"description\": \"No Content-Security-Policy or security headers for static files. Static assets served without X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, etc. Vulnerable to XSS attacks through HTML injection.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-693: Protection Mechanism Failure\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Add middleware to set security headers: add_middleware(HeadersMiddleware) with CSP, X-Frame-Options, etc.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/agents/orchestrator.py\",\n      \"line\": 148-154,\n      \"description\": \"Unsafe JSON parsing with lookahead truncation. Attempts to extract JSON from text by finding '{' and '}' characters. Could parse incorrect JSON if user input contains these characters.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-95: Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Use strict JSON parsing with try/except. Require LLM to output JSON in specific format via system prompt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/config.py\",\n      \"line\": 45-50,\n      \"description\": \"Environment variables override config without type coercion validation. PORT could be set to non-numeric value via SERVER_PORT env var causing TypeError.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-1025: Comparison Using Wrong Factors\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Validate env var values before use. Use pydantic-settings for automatic validation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api/routes.py, src/api/websocket.py\",\n      \"line\": \"multiple\",\n      \"description\": \"No rate limiting on API endpoints. Attackers can flood the system with requests, causing DoS.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Use slowapi or FastAPI middleware to limit requests: limiter = Limiter(key_func=get_remote_address)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/main.py\",\n      \"line\": \"27-40\",\n      \"description\": \"No CSRF token validation. POST endpoints accept requests from any origin without token verification.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Implement CSRF middleware with token validation or use SameSite cookie attribute.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/data/db.py\",\n      \"line\": \"358-368\",\n      \"description\": \"Batch delete query (clear_expired) uses string concatenation for TTL hours parameter. While using parameterized queries elsewhere, this specific datetime manipulation could be vulnerable.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-89: SQL Injection\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Verify TTL is numeric before using in SQL: assert isinstance(ttl_hours, int)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 72,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"IMMEDIATE (Critical): Implement authentication (OAuth2/JWT) and restrict CORS to specific domains\",\n    \"IMMEDIATE: Add authorization checks to verify users can only access their own data\",\n    \"URGENT: Deploy behind HTTPS reverse proxy and enforce secure transport\",\n    \"URGENT: Implement comprehensive input validation on all WebSocket messages and API parameters\",\n    \"HIGH: Sanitize error messages and add security headers (CSP, X-Frame-Options, etc.)\",\n    \"HIGH: Stop logging raw user input and LLM responses; log only sanitized data\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Add rate limiting to prevent DoS attacks\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Use strict JSON schema validation instead of regex parsing\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Implement CSRF protection and secure cookie settings\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Add database query owner validation (row-level security)\",\n    \"LOW: Use urllib.parse for URL handling instead of regex\",\n    \"LOW: Migrate config to environment variables with Pydantic validation\"\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The application has critical security gaps: no authentication, open CORS, and unencrypted HTTP transmission of sensitive HR policy data. Combined with missing authorization checks (IDOR vulnerability) and unvalidated WebSocket input, this system is vulnerable to unauthorized access, data exfiltration, and potential code injection. The application is NOT production-ready and should not be exposed to any network without immediate remediation of authentication and encryption.\"\n}\n```\n\n**Key Priority Actions:**\n\n1. **Add Authentication** - Require login before accessing any data\n2. **Restrict CORS** - Only allow requests from your domain  \n3. **Enable HTTPS** - Deploy behind an HTTPS reverse proxy immediately\n4. **Validate Inputs** - Add Pydantic schema validation to WebSocket and API endpoints\n5. **Secure Error Handling** - Return generic errors to users, log details server-side only\n\nWould you like me to implement security fixes for any of these vulnerabilities?\n",
